<!-- This is the `intent` region `verify-comment.mjs --section intent` writes into the PR's verify report.
     It is the only place the criteria appear: a table in a collapsed <details>, above the verdict. The report body
     never repeats them. Copy every criterion from .agent/{branch}/verify/intent.md verbatim; never reword one.
     No HTML comment inside the region: a reader cannot see one. Delete this comment when writing the file.
     Row grammar (parsed by parseIntent, no model):
       | <status>&nbsp;[🚀&nbsp;]AC‑n | <criterion text> | <kind>[:<target>] · <witnesses> · <links> |
       | 🛡️&nbsp;G‑n | <guardrail, verbatim from the brief> | guardrail |
     - The ID uses a non-breaking hyphen (U+2011) so it never wraps; `&nbsp;` joins mark and ID.
     - First publication: every AC starts ⬜ (not run). Later runs change only the leading mark (✅ ❌ ⏭️, 🚀)
       through `--marks`, which also refreshes the counts in the summary. Never reword a row.
     - Proof starts with the kind: ui, api, worker or telemetry. Write `api:PUT /api/x` (kind:target) for an
       api or worker criterion so the production watch can read its target.
     - Proof links are Dash0 deep links (traces explorer or trace), SHA-pinned test-file links, or screenshots.
     - Escape a literal | in a cell as \|. -->
<details><summary>📋 Acceptance criteria — {{N_AC}} criteria · {{N_G}} guardrails</summary>

